  "id": "COMPOUND:17084 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "Nyasicoside is implicated in the regulation of the inner centromere protein through a series of molecular interactions involving Jasplakinolide Z1, a known target of Nyasicoside. The evidence suggests that Nyasicoside acts as a modulator of Jasplakinolide Z1, which in turn targets the inner centromere protein. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, indicating a consistent and robust relationship across three distinct pathways. The shared involvement of Jasplakinolide Z1 as a mediator in these interactions implies a potential mechanism by which Nyasicoside influences the inner centromere protein, possibly through the inhibition of a downstream kinase or regulatory pathway. The presence of multiple independent evidence chains strengthens the likelihood of a functional relationship, although further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Nyasicoside in the regulation of the inner centromere protein.",
